# CPR for GMT24

`CPR` = commit, push, redeploy production. In this repo the redeploy is **Git-triggered**:
Vercel's GitHub integration builds every push to `main` as the production deployment
(project `7-l-advisory/gmt24`, alias `gmt24.vercel.app`).

- Do **not** run `npx vercel --prod`. The `Vercel_token` secret cannot access the
  `7-l-advisory` team (SAML-enforced; token returns 404/403), so the CLI path fails.
- After pushing `main`, confirm the deploy instead:
  `gh api repos/classichot/GMT24/deployments --jq '.[0]'` → newest `Production` entry
  should carry the pushed SHA; its statuses endpoint reports `success` plus the
  deployment URL. Then spot-check `https://gmt24.vercel.app`.
- Report: commit hash, push status, deployment SHA/status, production URL.
- PR merges into `main` are done locally (`git worktree` + `--no-ff` merge + push);
  the GitHub token cannot merge via API.
